  "note": "The comparison with Arabic ḥrr illustrates the image but uses a different final radical. The rare competitive stem may express rivalry stirred by anger. Harumaph contains the longer form חרומ, also compared with חָרוּם in Leviticus 21:18, so his name cannot securely be derived from חרה."
